itten notice of standard contract terms as part of a\nbundle that includes numerous other notices, including mandated warnings and\npromotional pamphlets. If the business does not take additional action to draw the\nconsumer's attention to the written notice of the standard contract terms, the requirement\nof reasonable notice is not satisfied, because the disclosure of the terms is overshadowed\nby the additional information. For the reasonable-notice requirement to be satisfied, the\nbusiness must take additional steps to draw the consumer's attention to the term, for\nexample, by segregating the disclosure of the terms from other materials, giving it more\n38\n@§2\n"